          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em sphere fiber bundle
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+bundle"} fiber bundle
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibers"} fibers
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spheres"} spheres
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^n
            of some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %p
            Often, but not always, this is considered in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            or even in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+theory"} stable homotopy theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibers"} fibers
            which have the (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+type"}> stable
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
            of a sphere, in which case one speaks of
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spherical+fibrations"} spherical fibrations
          %h2#Properties Properties
          %h3#VerticalTangentBundlesOfSphereBundles Vertical tangent bundles of sphere bundles
